1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,597
Sweetheart, in nineteen sixty-four,

2
00:00:02,597 --> 00:00:05,344
a flank steak cost forty-nine cents a

3
00:00:05,344 --> 00:00:08,090
pound, because nobody knew what to do

4
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:08,684
with it.

5
00:00:08,864 --> 00:00:09,691
It's a long,

6
00:00:09,691 --> 00:00:11,895
flat, lean cut from the belly of

7
00:00:11,895 --> 00:00:14,445
the cow, with the grain running right

8
00:00:14,445 --> 00:00:16,305
down it like the lines on a

9
00:00:16,305 --> 00:00:17,269
corduroy coat.

10
00:00:17,449 --> 00:00:18,428
Cook it wrong,

11
00:00:18,428 --> 00:00:20,944
and it's like chewing a rubber boot.

12
00:00:21,124 --> 00:00:22,135
Cook it right,

13
00:00:22,135 --> 00:00:24,300
and it's as tender as a filet,

14
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,105
for a third of the price.

15
00:00:26,455 --> 00:00:29,107
So tonight I'm giving you my marinated

16
00:00:29,107 --> 00:00:31,760
flank steak, a whole family supper for

17
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:33,295
about fifteen dollars,

18
00:00:33,295 --> 00:00:35,948
every step, and the five mistakes that

19
00:00:35,948 --> 00:00:37,623
make it tough and chewy.

20
00:00:37,803 --> 00:00:39,008
And stay with me,

21
00:00:39,008 --> 00:00:41,772
because the last mistake happens on the

22
00:00:41,772 --> 00:00:44,324
cutting board, and it's the one that

23
00:00:44,324 --> 00:00:45,245
matters most.

24
00:00:45,425 --> 00:00:48,152
You can do everything else right and

25
00:00:48,152 --> 00:00:50,348
still ruin it in ten seconds.

26
00:00:50,698 --> 00:00:52,689
When I was a young wife,

27
00:00:52,689 --> 00:00:55,759
the magazines called it London broil.

28
00:00:55,939 --> 00:00:58,111
There's nothing English about it,

29
00:00:58,111 --> 00:00:58,505
honey.

30
00:00:58,685 --> 00:01:00,617
It was just a fancy name the

31
00:01:00,617 --> 00:01:03,171
butchers used to sell the cheap flank

32
00:01:03,171 --> 00:01:03,585
steak.

33
00:01:03,765 --> 00:01:05,608
They'd marinate it,

34
00:01:05,608 --> 00:01:07,742
broil it hot and fast,

35
00:01:07,742 --> 00:01:09,488
and slice it thin.

36
00:01:09,668 --> 00:01:12,041
And every young wife in America made

37
00:01:12,041 --> 00:01:13,425
it on Saturday night,

38
00:01:13,425 --> 00:01:16,127
because it looked like a fancy restaurant

39
00:01:16,127 --> 00:01:16,588
dinner.

40
00:01:16,938 --> 00:01:18,760
The first time I made it,

41
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:21,093
I broiled it for twenty minutes,

42
00:01:21,093 --> 00:01:23,207
until it was gray all the way

43
00:01:23,207 --> 00:01:25,321
through, and sliced it thick,

44
00:01:25,321 --> 00:01:26,342
the wrong way.

45
00:01:26,522 --> 00:01:29,001
My husband chewed one bite for so

46
00:01:29,001 --> 00:01:31,630
long, I thought he'd fallen asleep.

47
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:34,051
He was too polite to say anything.

48
00:01:34,231 --> 00:01:35,854
The next morning,

49
00:01:35,854 --> 00:01:37,764
I asked the butcher,

50
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:38,050
Mr.

51
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:40,785
Albrecht, what I'd done wrong.

52
00:01:40,965 --> 00:01:43,217
He laughed for a full minute,

53
00:01:43,217 --> 00:01:44,459
then he told me.

54
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:45,680
Mr.

55
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,194
Albrecht's rules were simple.

56
00:01:48,374 --> 00:01:51,360
Marinate it, cook it hot and fast,

57
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:54,346
rest it, and slice it thin against

58
00:01:54,346 --> 00:01:55,224
the grain.

59
00:01:55,404 --> 00:01:57,306
In a minute I'll show you all

60
00:01:57,306 --> 00:01:57,830
of them.

61
00:01:58,010 --> 00:02:00,576
And today, flank steak is one of

62
00:02:00,576 --> 00:02:03,462
the most popular cuts in America for

63
00:02:03,462 --> 00:02:06,509
tacos, fajitas, salads and sandwiches.

64
00:02:06,689 --> 00:02:09,025
It's not forty-nine cents anymore,

65
00:02:09,025 --> 00:02:11,156
but it still feeds a family for

66
00:02:11,156 --> 00:02:12,668
less than steak night.

67
00:02:13,018 --> 00:02:14,842
Here's what you need,

68
00:02:14,842 --> 00:02:15,363
honey.

69
00:02:15,543 --> 00:02:16,947
One flank steak,

70
00:02:16,947 --> 00:02:19,317
about one and a half to two

71
00:02:19,317 --> 00:02:19,931
pounds.

72
00:02:20,111 --> 00:02:22,538
That feeds four to six people.

73
00:02:22,718 --> 00:02:24,212
For the marinade,

74
00:02:24,212 --> 00:02:26,584
a quarter cup of soy sauce.

75
00:02:26,764 --> 00:02:28,807
A quarter cup of olive oil.

76
00:02:28,987 --> 00:02:31,994
Two tablespoons of lemon juice or red

77
00:02:31,994 --> 00:02:33,051
wine vinegar.

78
00:02:33,231 --> 00:02:35,855
Two tablespoons of brown sugar.

79
00:02:36,035 --> 00:02:38,291
Three cloves of garlic,

80
00:02:38,291 --> 00:02:39,076
crushed.

81
00:02:39,256 --> 00:02:41,845
One teaspoon of black pepper.

82
00:02:42,025 --> 00:02:44,974
And a tablespoon of Worcestershire sauce.

83
00:02:45,324 --> 00:02:46,798
And when you buy it,

84
00:02:46,798 --> 00:02:49,083
look for a steak that's an even

85
00:02:49,083 --> 00:02:50,925
thickness, about an inch,

86
00:02:50,925 --> 00:02:52,841
from one end to the other,

87
00:02:52,841 --> 00:02:55,125
with bright red meat and only a

88
00:02:55,125 --> 00:02:55,936
little fat.

89
00:02:56,116 --> 00:02:58,141
If one end is much thinner,

90
00:02:58,141 --> 00:03:00,916
it'll overcook while the thick end is

91
00:03:00,916 --> 00:03:01,666
still raw.

92
00:03:01,846 --> 00:03:03,893
You can fold the thin end under,

93
00:03:03,893 --> 00:03:05,876
or pound the thick end a little

94
00:03:05,876 --> 00:03:06,964
with a heavy pan,

95
00:03:06,964 --> 00:03:07,987
to make it even.

96
00:03:08,338 --> 00:03:09,278
Step one.

97
00:03:09,458 --> 00:03:10,735
Score the steak.

98
00:03:10,915 --> 00:03:12,455
With a sharp knife,

99
00:03:12,455 --> 00:03:15,131
make shallow cuts across the top,

100
00:03:15,131 --> 00:03:17,725
about an eighth of an inch deep,

101
00:03:17,725 --> 00:03:19,428
in a diamond pattern,

102
00:03:19,428 --> 00:03:20,563
on both sides.

103
00:03:20,743 --> 00:03:23,028
That lets the marinade soak in,

104
00:03:23,028 --> 00:03:25,609
and it stops the steak from curling

105
00:03:25,609 --> 00:03:26,641
up in the pan.

106
00:03:26,821 --> 00:03:27,633
Mr.

107
00:03:27,813 --> 00:03:30,465
Albrecht did this for me the first

108
00:03:30,465 --> 00:03:30,855
time.

109
00:03:31,035 --> 00:03:33,462
Then I learned to do it myself.

110
00:03:33,812 --> 00:03:36,586
Whisk the marinade together in a bowl.

111
00:03:36,766 --> 00:03:39,012
Put the steak in a big zipper

112
00:03:39,012 --> 00:03:40,716
bag or a shallow dish,

113
00:03:40,716 --> 00:03:42,729
pour the marinade over it,

114
00:03:42,729 --> 00:03:44,278
and turn it to coat.

115
00:03:44,458 --> 00:03:46,087
Squeeze out the air,

116
00:03:46,087 --> 00:03:47,228
close the bag,

117
00:03:47,228 --> 00:03:49,264
and put it in the icebox.

118
00:03:49,444 --> 00:03:52,393
Mistake number one is skipping the marinade.

119
00:03:52,573 --> 00:03:54,045
Flank steak is lean,

120
00:03:54,045 --> 00:03:55,590
with very little fat,

121
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:58,238
and the marinade gives it flavor and

122
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,783
helps make it tender.

123
00:04:00,134 --> 00:04:01,457
How long?

124
00:04:01,637 --> 00:04:03,198
At least two hours,

125
00:04:03,198 --> 00:04:04,841
and up to overnight.

126
00:04:05,021 --> 00:04:07,309
But here's mistake number two.

127
00:04:07,489 --> 00:04:09,410
Marinating it too long,

128
00:04:09,410 --> 00:04:10,914
two or three days.

129
00:04:11,094 --> 00:04:13,348
The acid in the lemon or vinegar

130
00:04:13,348 --> 00:04:15,813
starts to break down the outside of

131
00:04:15,813 --> 00:04:18,067
the meat, and it turns mushy and

132
00:04:18,067 --> 00:04:18,419
gray.

133
00:04:18,599 --> 00:04:20,318
Overnight is plenty.

134
00:04:20,498 --> 00:04:22,473
I put mine in the bag after

135
00:04:22,473 --> 00:04:25,327
breakfast, and it's perfect for supper.

136
00:04:25,678 --> 00:04:26,931
Step two.

137
00:04:27,111 --> 00:04:29,317
Take the steak out of the icebox

138
00:04:29,317 --> 00:04:31,384
thirty minutes before cooking.

139
00:04:31,564 --> 00:04:33,928
Take it out of the marinade and

140
00:04:33,928 --> 00:04:36,521
pat it very dry with paper towels.

141
00:04:36,701 --> 00:04:39,311
Mistake number three is putting a wet

142
00:04:39,311 --> 00:04:40,509
steak in the pan.

143
00:04:40,689 --> 00:04:43,685
A wet steak steams and turns gray.

144
00:04:43,865 --> 00:04:46,402
A dry steak sears and gets a

145
00:04:46,402 --> 00:04:48,938
dark, delicious brown crust.

146
00:04:49,118 --> 00:04:51,452
Throw away the used marinade.

147
00:04:51,801 --> 00:04:53,507
If this is helping you,

148
00:04:53,507 --> 00:04:56,028
honey, tap the like button for me.

149
00:04:56,208 --> 00:04:58,855
It helps Grandma more than you know.

150
00:04:59,035 --> 00:05:01,336
Now heat a big cast iron skillet

151
00:05:01,336 --> 00:05:03,638
over high heat for five minutes,

152
00:05:03,638 --> 00:05:05,652
until it's smoking a little.

153
00:05:05,832 --> 00:05:07,740
Or heat your grill as hot as

154
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:09,988
it goes, or your broiler with the

155
00:05:09,988 --> 00:05:11,486
rack close to the top.

156
00:05:11,666 --> 00:05:13,360
Flank steak wants heat,

157
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,464
and lots of it.

158
00:05:14,644 --> 00:05:16,465
Add a spoon of oil to the

159
00:05:16,465 --> 00:05:17,048
skillet.

160
00:05:17,398 --> 00:05:19,214
Lay the steak in the pan,

161
00:05:19,214 --> 00:05:20,231
away from you,

162
00:05:20,231 --> 00:05:21,612
and don't touch it.

163
00:05:21,792 --> 00:05:23,943
Let it sear for four or five

164
00:05:23,943 --> 00:05:26,555
minutes, until it has a deep brown

165
00:05:26,555 --> 00:05:27,016
crust.

166
00:05:27,196 --> 00:05:28,512
Then flip it once,

167
00:05:28,512 --> 00:05:30,850
and cook it another four or five

168
00:05:30,850 --> 00:05:31,434
minutes.

169
00:05:31,614 --> 00:05:32,589
That's it.

170
00:05:32,769 --> 00:05:35,694
Mistake number four is cooking it too

171
00:05:35,694 --> 00:05:36,090
long.

172
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:38,798
Flank steak is best medium-rare,

173
00:05:38,798 --> 00:05:40,298
pink in the middle.

174
00:05:40,478 --> 00:05:41,888
Cook it well done,

175
00:05:41,888 --> 00:05:44,551
and no amount of slicing will save

176
00:05:44,551 --> 00:05:44,786
it.

177
00:05:45,136 --> 00:05:47,075
Use a meat thermometer,

178
00:05:47,075 --> 00:05:48,003
sweetheart.

179
00:05:48,183 --> 00:05:49,974
Take it off the heat at one

180
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:52,892
hundred thirty degrees in the thickest part,

181
00:05:52,892 --> 00:05:56,008
for medium-rare, or one thirty-five for medium.

182
00:05:56,188 --> 00:05:58,834
It keeps cooking a few degrees as

183
00:05:58,834 --> 00:05:59,555
it rests.

184
00:05:59,735 --> 00:06:02,353
If somebody in your family wants it

185
00:06:02,353 --> 00:06:04,897
well done, give them the thin end,

186
00:06:04,897 --> 00:06:06,318
which cooks faster.

187
00:06:06,498 --> 00:06:09,163
My brother Danny always got the thin

188
00:06:09,163 --> 00:06:09,459
end.

189
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:11,783
He thought it was because he was

190
00:06:11,783 --> 00:06:12,588
my favorite.

191
00:06:12,938 --> 00:06:15,061
And if you're using the broiler,

192
00:06:15,061 --> 00:06:16,853
like we did in the sixties,

193
00:06:16,853 --> 00:06:18,712
put the rack so the steak is

194
00:06:18,712 --> 00:06:20,902
about three inches from the heat.

195
00:06:21,082 --> 00:06:23,574
Line the pan with foil for easy

196
00:06:23,574 --> 00:06:24,298
cleaning.

197
00:06:24,478 --> 00:06:27,291
Broil it about five minutes a side,

198
00:06:27,291 --> 00:06:28,979
and watch it closely,

199
00:06:28,979 --> 00:06:31,792
because broilers are all different.

200
00:06:31,972 --> 00:06:34,757
Mine sets off the smoke alarm every

201
00:06:34,757 --> 00:06:37,463
single time, so I open the kitchen

202
00:06:37,463 --> 00:06:38,497
window first.

203
00:06:38,677 --> 00:06:40,929
The neighbors know it's steak night.

204
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:42,452
Step three.

205
00:06:42,632 --> 00:06:45,014
Put the steak on a cutting board,

206
00:06:45,014 --> 00:06:46,963
cover it loosely with foil,

207
00:06:46,963 --> 00:06:49,273
and let it rest for ten minutes.

208
00:06:49,453 --> 00:06:51,438
Don't cut it right away.

209
00:06:51,618 --> 00:06:53,957
The juices need time to settle back

210
00:06:53,957 --> 00:06:54,892
into the meat.

211
00:06:55,072 --> 00:06:56,399
If you cut it hot,

212
00:06:56,399 --> 00:06:58,758
all that juice runs out onto the

213
00:06:58,758 --> 00:07:01,116
board, and the meat on the plate

214
00:07:01,116 --> 00:07:01,632
is dry.

215
00:07:01,812 --> 00:07:04,227
Use those ten minutes to set the

216
00:07:04,227 --> 00:07:04,680
table.

217
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:06,447
So far, score it,

218
00:07:06,447 --> 00:07:09,533
marinate it overnight but not longer,

219
00:07:09,533 --> 00:07:10,451
pat it dry,

220
00:07:10,451 --> 00:07:12,202
sear it hot and fast,

221
00:07:12,202 --> 00:07:14,371
take it off at one thirty,

222
00:07:14,371 --> 00:07:16,372
and rest it ten minutes.

223
00:07:16,552 --> 00:07:19,083
Now the last mistake I promised you,

224
00:07:19,083 --> 00:07:21,543
the one that happens on the cutting

225
00:07:21,543 --> 00:07:23,019
board in ten seconds.

226
00:07:23,199 --> 00:07:24,825
It's the one Mr.

227
00:07:25,005 --> 00:07:27,060
Albrecht laughed about.

228
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:29,248
Slicing it the wrong way.

229
00:07:29,599 --> 00:07:31,000
Look at the steak,

230
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:31,468
honey.

231
00:07:31,648 --> 00:07:34,269
You'll see long lines running down it,

232
00:07:34,269 --> 00:07:36,063
from one end to the other,

233
00:07:36,063 --> 00:07:38,132
like the threads in a piece of

234
00:07:38,132 --> 00:07:38,753
corduroy.

235
00:07:38,933 --> 00:07:40,399
That's the grain,

236
00:07:40,399 --> 00:07:41,952
the muscle fibers.

237
00:07:42,132 --> 00:07:45,415
Mistake number five is slicing along those

238
00:07:45,415 --> 00:07:47,136
lines, with the grain.

239
00:07:47,316 --> 00:07:49,925
Then every slice is made of long,

240
00:07:49,925 --> 00:07:52,850
stringy fibers, and you chew and chew

241
00:07:52,850 --> 00:07:53,562
and chew.

242
00:07:53,742 --> 00:07:56,325
That's what my husband was doing for

243
00:07:56,325 --> 00:07:56,900
so long.

244
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:59,848
Instead, turn the steak so the lines

245
00:07:59,848 --> 00:08:01,941
run left to right in front of

246
00:08:01,941 --> 00:08:02,230
you.

247
00:08:02,410 --> 00:08:04,405
Then slice across them,

248
00:08:04,405 --> 00:08:05,966
against the grain,

249
00:08:05,966 --> 00:08:07,441
into thin slices,

250
00:08:07,441 --> 00:08:09,783
about a quarter of an inch.

251
00:08:09,963 --> 00:08:12,231
Hold your knife at a slant,

252
00:08:12,231 --> 00:08:15,257
almost flat, so the slices are wide.

253
00:08:15,437 --> 00:08:18,038
Now every slice has only short little

254
00:08:18,038 --> 00:08:20,429
fibers, and it's tender as butter.

255
00:08:20,609 --> 00:08:22,467
Same steak, sweetheart.

256
00:08:22,647 --> 00:08:24,760
Just a different direction.

257
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:27,452
Lay the slices on a warm platter,

258
00:08:27,452 --> 00:08:29,937
fanned out, and pour any juice from

259
00:08:29,937 --> 00:08:31,925
the cutting board over them.

260
00:08:32,105 --> 00:08:34,547
Sprinkle with a little coarse salt and

261
00:08:34,547 --> 00:08:35,576
chopped parsley.

262
00:08:35,756 --> 00:08:38,503
I serve it with baked potatoes and

263
00:08:38,503 --> 00:08:39,634
a green salad.

264
00:08:39,814 --> 00:08:42,937
Or roasted potatoes and green beans.

265
00:08:43,117 --> 00:08:46,046
My husband liked a spoon of horseradish

266
00:08:46,046 --> 00:08:47,398
sauce on the side,

267
00:08:47,398 --> 00:08:49,652
and he never chewed for a full

268
00:08:49,652 --> 00:08:50,628
minute again.

269
00:08:50,979 --> 00:08:52,582
And the leftovers,

270
00:08:52,582 --> 00:08:54,810
honey, are the best part.

271
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:57,656
Thin slices of cold flank steak on

272
00:08:57,656 --> 00:09:00,714
a sandwich with horseradish and onions.

273
00:09:00,894 --> 00:09:03,149
Or warm them in a skillet with

274
00:09:03,149 --> 00:09:05,479
peppers and onions for fajitas.

275
00:09:05,659 --> 00:09:07,843
Or on top of a green salad

276
00:09:07,843 --> 00:09:09,270
with blue cheese.

277
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:12,364
My granddaughter makes steak tacos with it

278
00:09:12,364 --> 00:09:15,000
every Tuesday, with lime and cilantro.

279
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:17,908
It keeps three days in the icebox.

280
00:09:18,258 --> 00:09:20,543
And you can change the marinade any

281
00:09:20,543 --> 00:09:21,392
way you like.

282
00:09:21,572 --> 00:09:23,570
For a Mexican flavor,

283
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:24,997
use lime juice,

284
00:09:24,997 --> 00:09:27,946
cumin, chili powder and garlic.

285
00:09:28,126 --> 00:09:30,047
For an Asian flavor,

286
00:09:30,047 --> 00:09:31,775
soy sauce, ginger,

287
00:09:31,775 --> 00:09:33,792
sesame oil and honey.

288
00:09:33,972 --> 00:09:35,898
For an Italian flavor,

289
00:09:35,898 --> 00:09:38,350
balsamic vinegar, olive oil,

290
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:40,102
rosemary and garlic.

291
00:09:40,282 --> 00:09:43,347
The method stays exactly the same.

292
00:09:43,527 --> 00:09:45,682
Marinade, hot and fast,

293
00:09:45,682 --> 00:09:48,867
rest, and slice against the grain.

294
00:09:49,218 --> 00:09:50,831
So one more time.

295
00:09:51,011 --> 00:09:52,542
Buy an even steak,

296
00:09:52,542 --> 00:09:53,647
and score it.

297
00:09:53,827 --> 00:09:55,731
Marinate it overnight,

298
00:09:55,731 --> 00:09:56,683
not longer.

299
00:09:56,863 --> 00:09:59,098
Take it out early and pat it

300
00:09:59,098 --> 00:09:59,417
dry.

301
00:09:59,597 --> 00:10:01,483
Sear it hot and fast,

302
00:10:01,483 --> 00:10:03,997
four or five minutes a side.

303
00:10:04,177 --> 00:10:06,197
Take it off at one thirty.

304
00:10:06,377 --> 00:10:08,107
Rest it ten minutes.

305
00:10:08,287 --> 00:10:09,802
And slice it thin,

306
00:10:09,802 --> 00:10:11,317
against the grain.

307
00:10:11,497 --> 00:10:12,867
That's how Mr.

308
00:10:13,047 --> 00:10:14,444
Albrecht taught me,

309
00:10:14,444 --> 00:10:16,797
and it's never been tough since.

310
00:10:17,148 --> 00:10:19,098
Tell me in the comments,

311
00:10:19,098 --> 00:10:19,992
sweetheart.

312
00:10:20,172 --> 00:10:22,865
Did your family call it London broil?

313
00:10:23,045 --> 00:10:25,473
And what's your favorite way to eat

314
00:10:25,473 --> 00:10:25,681
it?

315
00:10:25,861 --> 00:10:29,009
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

316
00:10:29,009 --> 00:10:31,033
right there on your screen,

317
00:10:31,033 --> 00:10:33,132
and I'll see you in the next

318
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:33,582
video.

319
00:10:33,762 --> 00:10:35,352
Good night, honey.
